From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: cv1800: print the cam0_200 clock state at probe

Diagnostic only: the console goes silent right after the bootconsole
handover, so we cannot see whether the bootloader left cam0_200 on the
crystal or on disppll/div. Print the divider/mux, bypass, gate and
disppll CSR registers once at probe, with keep_bootcon on the command
line so the earlycon keeps printing.

--- a/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv1800.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv1800.c
@@ -1525,7 +1525,12 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	return cv1800_clk_init_ctrl(dev, reg, ctrl, desc);
+	ret = cv1800_clk_init_ctrl(dev, reg, ctrl, desc);
+	if (!ret)
+		pr_info("rnsbox-clk: div_cam0_200=0x%08x byp0=0x%08x en1=0x%08x disppll_csr=0x%08x%c",
+			readl(reg + 0x0A8), readl(reg + 0x030), readl(reg + 0x004),
+			readl(reg + 0x810), 10);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id cv1800_clk_ids[] = {
